@startuml livevox-passthrough-call-flow
title proAgent escalation to a human agent — Twilio → LiveKit → jambonz → LiveVox STG4

skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
skinparam BoxPadding 8

actor "PSTN caller" as Caller

box "Ingress (test setup)" #F4F7FB
  participant "Twilio\nSIP trunk" as Twilio
end box

box "LiveKit" #F7F4FB
  participant "LiveKit SIP\nservice" as LKSIP
  participant "proAgent\napplication" as ProAgent
end box

box "jambonz — eu.jambonz.io" #F4FBF6
  participant "SBC\n(sbc-inbound /\nsbc-outbound)" as SBC
  participant "feature-server" as FS
  participant "livevox-passthrough\napp (ws :3101)" as App
  participant "rtpengine" as RTP
end box

box "LiveVox" #FBF7F4
  participant "LiveVox STG4" as LiveVox
end box

autonumber "<b>[00]"

== 1. Inbound PSTN leg reaches proAgent ==

Caller -> Twilio : PSTN call to DID
Twilio -> LKSIP : INVITE (Twilio Elastic SIP trunk)
LKSIP --> Twilio : 200 OK
LKSIP -> ProAgent : participant joined (room event)
note over Caller, ProAgent
  Caller is now in a LiveKit room with proAgent.
  Media: Caller <-> Twilio <-> LiveKit <-> proAgent
end note

== 2. proAgent decides to escalate to a human ==

ProAgent -> ProAgent : escalation decision
ProAgent -> LKSIP : CreateSIPParticipant\n(outbound trunk -> jambonz SIP URI)\nheaders: X-LiveVox-Destination,\nX-LiveVox-Session-Id, X-Prodigal-*

== 3. jambonz receives the INVITE and picks the LiveVox trunk ==

LKSIP -> SBC : INVITE sip:<number>@eu.jambonz.io\nX-LiveVox-Destination: +1899...\nX-LiveVox-Session-Id: ...\n(Diversion header ignored downstream)
SBC --> LKSIP : 100 Trying
note right of SBC
  LiveKit is authorized as a **carrier** on
  its source IP; the dialed DID is mapped to
  the jambonz **application** whose URL is
  ws://127.0.0.1:3101/
end note
SBC -> FS : route to application
FS -> App : session:new\n(includes raw INVITE in data.sip.headers\nand portal env_vars)

App -> App : resolve destination\n1. X-LiveVox-Destination\n2. X-Prodigal-Destination\n3. dialed number (to)\n4. env_vars.LIVEVOX_NUMBER\n(Diversion never consulted)
App -> App : collect every inbound\nX-LiveVox* / X-Prodigal* header

App -> FS : dial verb\nanswerOnBridge: true, **anchorMedia: false**, timeout: 30\ncallerId: **session.from** (original caller passed through)\nheaders: <forwarded X- headers>\ntarget: [{ type: phone, number, **trunk: env CARRIER** }]

note over App, FS #FFF6D6
  **This is where the LiveVox trunk is chosen.**
  LiveKit does not and cannot select the trunk — it
  only reaches a jambonz DID. Trunk selection is
  `target[].trunk`, fed by the CARRIER application
  variable (default "Livevox - staging"), so
  staging -> production is a portal change.
end note

== 4. Outbound leg to LiveVox over mTLS ==

FS -> SBC : outbound call request (trunk = CARRIER)
SBC -> LiveVox : INVITE over **TLS (mTLS, client cert)**\nSDP offer: **SRTP-SDES**\nforwarded X-LiveVox* / X-Prodigal* headers
LiveVox --> SBC : 100 Trying
LiveVox --> SBC : 200 OK (answers to play announcement)
SBC -> LiveVox : ACK

SBC -> FS : outbound leg answered
FS -> SBC : answer inbound leg (answerOnBridge)
SBC --> LKSIP : 200 OK (LiveVox SDP relayed)
LKSIP -> SBC : ACK

note over RTP #FFE0E0
  **anchorMedia: false** — rtpengine is released from
  the media path once the legs are bridged. Media goes
  LiveKit <-> LiveVox directly, so both ends must agree
  on codecs and on crypto (SRTP-SDES vs plain RTP)
  without jambonz translating between them.
end note

LiveVox -> LKSIP : RTP/SRTP announcement **direct**:\n"the number you have dialed\nis not in service"
LKSIP -> ProAgent : audio of announcement

== 5. LiveVox tears the leg down; BYE propagates back ==

LiveVox -> SBC : BYE (announcement finished)
SBC --> LiveVox : 200 OK
SBC -> FS : outbound leg ended
FS -> App : verb:hook /dial-complete\ndial_call_status, dial_sip_status, duration
App -> FS : hangup
FS -> SBC : end inbound leg
SBC -> LKSIP : BYE
LKSIP --> SBC : 200 OK

LKSIP -> ProAgent : SIP participant disconnected
ProAgent -> ProAgent : clean up call resources
ProAgent -> LKSIP : (optional) close room / drop caller
LKSIP -> Twilio : BYE
Twilio -> Caller : call cleared

@enduml
